export anchor AsdSte100:
    base:
        Write in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.

        This rule applies while this skill is in use. It does not stop when the
        topic changes.

        - Use approved words. Use one word for one meaning.
        - Write technical names, commands and code as they are.
        - Write 20 words or fewer in an instruction and 25 words or fewer in a
            description.
        - Write one topic in each sentence and in each paragraph.
        - Use the active voice and the simple present, past or future tense.
        - Use the imperative for instructions.
        - Do not use -ing forms, contractions or phrasal verbs.
        - Use articles. Write noun clusters of 3 words or fewer.
        - Write literally. Do not use idioms or figures of speech.
        - Use a vertical list for steps and for facts that have the same shape.

        The instructions of the skill decide what a reply must contain. Keep all
        of it, and write it in ASD-STE100.
